        </ns1:item>
    
        <ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-02867-w">
            <ns1:title>Daily briefing: OpenAI claims a huge maths breakthrough</ns1:title>
            <ns1:link>https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-02867-w</ns1:link>
            <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature, Published online: 09 September 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-02867-w"&gt;doi:10.1038/d41586-026-02867-w&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;The AI giant claims to have solved one of maths’ trickiest problems, but questions swirl over should get the credit. Plus, an atlas of every single DNA letter mutation in humans and why more bioengineered microorganisms aren’t making it out of the lab.</content:encoded>
            <dc:title>Daily briefing: OpenAI claims a huge maths breakthrough</dc:title>
            <dc:creator>Flora Graham</dc:creator>
            <dc:identifier>doi:10.1038/d41586-026-02867-w</dc:identifier>
            <dc:source>Nature, Published online: 2026-09-09; | doi:10.1038/d41586-026-02867-w</dc:source>
            <dc:date>2026-09-09</dc:date>
            <ns4:publicationName>Nature</ns4:publicationName>
            <ns4:doi>10.1038/d41586-026-02867-w</ns4:doi>
